Description: Specify mixed models using familiar ASReml or brms-style formula
    syntax and estimate them via greta or INLA. Returns results in formats
    compatible with the standard R modelling ecosystem including 'summary()',
    'emmeans', 'marginaleffects', and 'effectsize'. The package translates
    ASReml-style formulas (fixed, random, rcov) to backend-specific code
    (greta or INLA) using an indexing approach that scales to large
    agricultural datasets, and supports cross-engine posterior triangulation
    as a robustness signal. Supports Gaussian, binomial, Poisson, negative
    binomial, gamma, and beta families, as well as structured covariance
    models (us, fa, ar1), genomic relationship matrices (GBLUP),
    pedigree-based models, spatial models, and splines.
